---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import AtmosphereBg from "../components/AtmosphereBg.astro";
import Nav from "../components/Nav.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";

const lastUpdated = "2026-04-25";
---

<Layout
  title="Terms of Service · tKids"
  description="The rules for using tkids.tw — what you can and can't do, who is allowed, and what happens if things go wrong."
  lang="en"
  noindex={false}
>
  <AtmosphereBg />
  <Nav />

  <main class="terms">
    <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
    <p class="meta">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

    <p class="lede">
      These terms govern your use of <a href="https://tkids.tw">tkids.tw</a>
      (the <strong>"Site"</strong>), the official home of tKids — a music
      project featuring Ethan, Alan, and Albert. By using the Site, you
      agree to these terms.
    </p>

    <h2>1. Who can use the Site</h2>
    <p>
      The Site is intended for people aged 13 and older. If you are
      between 13 and 17, you may browse and play teasers, but creating
      an account, donating, leaving comments, or purchasing requires you
      to confirm you are 13 or older and to have a parent or guardian's
      permission where local law requires it. If you are under 13,
      please do not create an account or submit personal information.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Your account</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        One person, one account. Don't create accounts for other people
        without their permission, and don't share your account credentials.
      </li>
      <li>
        The information you provide during signup or onboarding (birth
        year, display name, locale, handle) must be accurate.
      </li>
      <li>
        You are responsible for activity that happens under your account.
        Tell us at <a href="mailto:hello@tkids.tw">hello@tkids.tw</a>
        immediately if you suspect unauthorized access.
      </li>
      <li>
        We may suspend or close accounts that violate these terms, attempt
        to circumvent our age gate, or abuse the Site.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>3. How you may use the Site</h2>
    <p>You may:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Listen to teasers and other audio we make available for streaming.</li>
      <li>Read journal posts, browse member pages, and use the fortune draw.</li>
      <li>Share links to public pages on social media.</li>
      <li>
        With an account: donate, leave comments where the feature is
        enabled, and purchase merchandise where available.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>4. How you may not use the Site</h2>
    <p>You agree not to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Impersonate Ethan, Alan, Albert, the tKids team, or any other
        user. This includes display names, avatars, and handles that
        could mislead others.
      </li>
      <li>
        Re-upload, redistribute, or commercially use any music, lyrics,
        artwork, video, or photo we publish on the Site without our
        written permission.
      </li>
      <li>
        Scrape, mass-download, or otherwise extract Site content using
        automated tools.
      </li>
      <li>
        Probe, attack, or attempt to bypass the security, rate limits,
        age gate, or moderation systems of the Site.
      </li>
      <li>
        Post comments or submit content that is harassing, hateful,
        sexual, threatening, defamatory, infringing, or illegal under
        Taiwanese law or the law of your jurisdiction.
      </li>
      <li>
        Use the Site to send unsolicited messages, advertise unrelated
        products, or run schemes targeting other fans.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>5. Content ownership</h2>
    <p>
      All music, lyrics, artwork, photos, video, and design on the Site
      are owned by tKids or our licensors and are protected by copyright
      and trademark law in Taiwan and internationally. You receive no
      rights in this content beyond the limited right to listen, view,
      and share links during your use of the Site.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Your contributions</h2>
    <p>
      When you submit content to the Site (for example a comment,
      profile bio, or display name), you keep ownership of what you
      submit, but you grant tKids a worldwide, non-exclusive,
      royalty-free license to host, display, translate, and moderate
      that content as part of running the Site. You confirm that you
      have the right to grant this license and that your contribution
      doesn't infringe anyone else's rights.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Donations and purchases</h2>
    <p>
      Donations are processed through our payment partner Polar. They
      are voluntary contributions to support the project and are
      non-refundable except where required by law. Merchandise (when
      available) is governed by the order confirmation and shipping
      terms shown at checkout.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Sign-in with Google</h2>
    <p>
      If you choose to sign in with Google, you authorize Google to share
      your name, email address, and Google profile picture with tKids.
      We use only the email and name; your Google profile picture is
      discarded and replaced with a generated avatar. Your relationship
      with Google is governed by Google's own terms.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Reporting abuse and copyright takedowns</h2>
    <p>
      To report a comment, account, or other content that violates these
      terms, email <a href="mailto:hello@tkids.tw">hello@tkids.tw</a>.
      To report copyright infringement, email
      <a href="mailto:hello@tkids.tw">hello@tkids.tw</a> with: the
      copyrighted work, the URL of the infringing material, your contact
      information, and a statement that you are authorized to act on the
      copyright owner's behalf. We respond to valid notices within 14
      days.
    </p>

    <h2>10. Service availability</h2>
    <p>
      The Site is provided "as is." We work to keep it online but we
      don't guarantee uninterrupted access, and we may add, change, or
      remove features at any time. Scheduled launches may be delayed for
      reasons outside our control.
    </p>

    <h2>11. Limitation of liability</h2>
    <p>
      To the fullest extent permitted by law, tKids and its members are
      not liable for any indirect, incidental, or consequential damages
      arising from your use of the Site. Where liability cannot be
      excluded, our total liability is limited to the amount you paid us
      in the twelve months before the claim, or NT$1,000, whichever is
      greater.
    </p>

    <h2>12. Termination</h2>
    <p>
      You can close your account at any time from the danger zone in
      your account settings. We can suspend or close your account with
      notice if you violate these terms or if we are required to by
      law. Closing your account ends your right to use the authenticated
      features of the Site; sections of these terms that should survive
      (ownership, liability, governing law) remain in effect.
    </p>

    <h2>13. Governing law</h2>
    <p>
      These terms are governed by the laws of the Republic of China
      (Taiwan), without regard to conflict-of-law rules. Disputes are
      subject to the exclusive jurisdiction of the Taipei District
      Court, except where local consumer-protection law gives you a
      stronger right.
    </p>

    <h2>14. Changes</h2>
    <p>
      We may update these terms. When we do, we'll post the new version
      here and update the "last updated" date. If a change materially
      reduces your rights, we'll notify account holders by email at
      least 14 days before the change takes effect. Continued use of
      the Site after the effective date is your acceptance of the new
      terms.
    </p>

    <h2>15. Severability and entire agreement</h2>
    <p>
      If any part of these terms is found unenforceable, the rest stays
      in effect. These terms, together with our
      <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>, are the entire agreement
      between you and tKids regarding the Site.
    </p>

    <h2>16. Contact</h2>
    <address>
      tKids · Taipei, Taiwan<br />
      <a href="mailto:hello@tkids.tw">hello@tkids.tw</a><br />
      <a href="mailto:privacy@tkids.tw">privacy@tkids.tw</a>
    </address>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Layout>

<style>
  .terms {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
    max-width: 720px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 140px 40px 120px;
    color: var(--chrome);
    font-family: "JetBrains Mono", monospace;
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }
  .terms h1 {
    font-family: "Unbounded", sans-serif;
    font-weight: 800;
    font-size: clamp(40px, 5vw, 64px);
    letter-spacing: -0.04em;
    color: var(--white);
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }
  .terms h2 {
    font-family: "Unbounded", sans-serif;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 18px;
    color: var(--white);
    margin-top: 36px;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }
  .terms .meta {
    font-size: 11px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.25em;
    color: var(--ice);
    opacity: 0.65;
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }
  .terms .lede {
    font-family: "DM Serif Display", serif;
    font-size: 22px;
    line-height: 1.45;
    color: var(--white);
    margin-bottom: 32px;
  }
  .terms p,
  .terms ul {
    margin-bottom: 18px;
  }
  .terms ul {
    padding-left: 22px;
  }
  .terms li {
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }
  .terms a {
    color: var(--glow);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }
  .terms a:hover {
    color: var(--gold);
  }
  .terms address {
    font-style: normal;
    margin-top: 12px;
    padding: 20px;
    border: 1px solid rgba(184, 204, 255, 0.15);
    border-radius: 12px;
  }

  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .terms {
      padding: 120px 20px 100px;
    }
  }
</style>
